// The tail of parse_decl, split off because decl/declare.id is already full, and
// the `blank` statement, which belongs with the statement forms rather than
// with the dispatch that routes to it.

// A bare keyword statement: `blank` or `break`. Both carry no operand, so the
// node is a leaf whose kind is the keyword itself.
//
// `blank` costs one action and does nothing. Its only use is to fill a segment
// that must reach three actions before a chain, in the case where the chain's
// first action cannot be lifted into that segment because the action following
// it is structurally tied to it -- an if/else-if chain being the instance,
// since splitting one would leave the chain unable to be spun back out into
// its own function later.
//
// `break` leaves the innermost enclosing `while` and costs no action. Outside
// every while it has nothing to leave, which is refused here, at the keyword.
parse_blank(int[] pos) {
  string bare_kw = cur_text(pos);
  if(bare_kw == "break" && (import loopd)[0] == 0) {
    syn_err(pos, "'break' is not inside a 'while': it leaves the innermost enclosing loop, so it can only appear in a while body");
  }
  advance(pos);
} chain (int[] pos) {
  skip_semi(pos);
  int ret_i = newleaf(bare_kw, 0 - 1, 0, "", "");
} return int ret_i;
